From 71d445eae26e22f9791a9bca7b72353312c78613 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:39:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 85/85] hw/sensor: MCP9600 thermocouple converter and the
 Thermo K Click

The MCP9600 (DS20005426F section 5): TH, TDELTA and TC in 1/16 degree
(TC at 0.25 degree on request), the raw ADC at 18 to 12 bits, STATUS
with TH Update, Burst Complete and Input Range, conversions at the ADC
resolution's rate in normal, shutdown and burst modes, four alerts
(TH or TC, rising or falling with hysteresis, comparator or latched
interrupt mode, push-pull with either polarity), and the device ID.
QOM "temperature" (hot junction) and "cold" (cold junction) in
milli-degrees; the raw ADC approximates the type K EMF as 41 uV per
degree.

Thermo K Click v102: 0x60 (ADDR on ground), ALERT1 on INT, ALERT2 on
PWM, ALERT3 on RST, ALERT4 on AN (the schematic, and MikroElektronika's
driver's map), no pull resistors.

qtests: ID, the temperatures and raw ADC after a conversion, clearing
TH Update, a rising ALERT1 on INT and its release, a negative
temperature on the MC00's EXT1; TH through TWI0 on the AVR64EA48 Nano
Base.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
